Email Subject:\
Urgent: Your account will be suspended today\
\
Sender:\
support@paypa1-security.example.com\
\
Targeted Brand:\
PayPal\
\
Suspicious Indicators:\
1. Sender domain uses "paypa1" instead of "paypal".\
2. Email uses urgent language to pressure the user.\
3. The message asks the user to verify account details.\
4. The link does not point to the official PayPal domain.\
5. Generic greeting: "Dear Customer".\
6. Threat of account suspension is used to create fear.\
\
Potential Impact:\
The user may enter login details into a fake website, allowing attackers to steal credentials.\
\
SOC Analyst Conclusion:\
This email should be treated as a phishing attempt. The user should not click the link, should not enter credentials, and should report the email to the security team.}